{title: 043 - When Morning Gilds the Skies}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #043 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 43}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]When [Cm]morning [Eb]guilds [Cm]the [F7]skies, [Gm]My [F7/A]heart [Gm/Bb]awaking cries,
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ be [F]praised!
[F7/Eb]Alike [Bb/D]at [F7/C]work and prayer, [Bb/D]To Jesus [F]I [F7/C]repair;
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]be praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Whene'er [Dm]the [Eb]sweet [Cm]church [F7]bell [Gm]peals [F7/A]over [F/A]hill [Gm]and dell,
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ praised!
[F7/Eb]O [Bb/D]hark to [Eb/Bb]what [F7/A]it sings, [Bb]as [F/C]joyously [F7/C]it [Bb]rings,
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]be praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]The [Cm]night [Dm]becomes [F7]as [Gm]day [F7/A]when [Gm/Bb]from [F/A]the [Gm]heart we [Cm]say:
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ be [F]praised!
[F7/Eb]The [Bb/D]powers [F7/C]of [Eb/Bb]darkness [F7/Eb]fear [Bb]when [F/C]this [C7]sweet [F]chant [F7/C]they [Bb]hear:
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]be praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Ye [Cm]nations [Eb]of [Cm]mankind, [Gm]in [F7/A]this [Gm/Bb]your [F/A]concord [Gm]find,
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ praised!
[F7/Eb]Let [Bb/D]all the [Eb/Bb]earth [F7/A]around [Bb]ring [F/C]joyous [C7]with [F7/C]the [Bb]sound,
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Bb]In heaven's [Dm]eternal [F7]bliss [Gm]the [F7/A]loveliest [Gm]strain is [Cm]this,
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ praised!
[F7/Eb]Let [Bb/D]earth, and [F7/C]sea and sky [Bb/D]from depth [C7]to [F]height [F7/C]reply,
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]praised!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[Bb]Be [Cm]this, [Dm]while [Cm]life [F7]is [Gm]mine, [F7/A]my [Gm/Bb]canticle divine:
[C7/E]May [F]Jesus [Cm]Christ be [F]praised!
[F7/Eb]Be [Bb/D]this th'eternal [F7/Eb]song [Bb/D]through all [C7]the [F]ages [Bb]long,
[Gm]May Jesus [F7]Christ [Bb]be praised!
{end_of_verse}
